{"title":"With hopes of victory fading, Ukraine's fight against Russia could get even harder in 2024 (Cnbc | World Business News Leader, 2023-12-25T23:36:00+00:00)","text":"With hopes of victory fading, Ukraine's fight against Russia could get even harder in 2024 (Cnbc | World Business News Leader, 2023-12-25T23:36:00+00:00)
A Ukrainian soldier is seen inside an artillery vehicle in his fighting position as Russia-Ukraine war continues in the direction of Kharkiv, Ukraine on November 20, 2023. Diego Herrera Carcedo | Anadolu | Getty Images

At the start of 2023, hopes were high that a much-vaunted Ukrainian counteroffensive — expected to be launched in the spring — would change the dial in the war against Russia. It didn't, and the prospect of a breakthrough in 2024 is also unlikely, military experts and defense analysts told CNBC. They predict intense fighting is likely to continue into the next year but say Kyiv's forces are unlikely to launch any more counteroffensives. Russia, meanwhile, is likely to focus on consolidating the territory it has already seized, particularly in eastern Ukraine.","entities":["Getty Images","Russia","Ukraine","CNBC","Ukrainian counteroffensive","Kyiv","Kharkiv","Diego Herrera Carcedo","Anadolu","Russia-Ukraine war","With hopes of victory fading, Ukraine's fight against Russia could get even harder in 2024"],"facts":["Which M.L.B. Playoff Team Has the Most Daunting Home Field? We Ranked Them. -MENTIONS-> Getty Images","Video games in 2023: Acquisitions, layoffs, unions -MENTIONS-> Getty Images","From Justin Timberlake to Sam Asghari: A timeline of Britney Spears’ relationships -MENTIONS-> Getty Images","West Indies v England: fifth and deciding men’s T20 cricket international – live -MENTIONS-> Getty Images","Amazon sellers sound off on the FTC's 'long-overdue' antitrust case -MENTIONS-> Getty Images"]}

{"title":"Hitting the Books: We are the frogs in the boiling pot, it's time we started governing like it. (Engadget, 2023-10-01T14:30:34+00:00)","text":"Hitting the Books: We are the frogs in the boiling pot, it's time we started governing like it. (Engadget, 2023-10-01T14:30:34+00:00)
The twenty-first century is also about the struggle against new and rising forms of authoritarianism. In this narration, the twenty-first century began with a wave of crushed democratic uprisings and continued with the election of authoritarian leaders around the world who began to dismantle democratic institutions. Any illusion of the success of globalization, or of the twenty-first century representing a break from the brutal twentieth century, was stripped away with Russia’s most recent invasion of Ukraine. The plot is less clear, given the failure of democracy-building efforts in the twentieth century. There is a faintly discernable storyline of general resistance and rebuilding imperfect democracies.

There’s also a third story about this century: the penetration of the Internet into every sphere of daily, social, and political life. Despite turn-of-the-century talk about the Information Age, we are only beginning to conceptualize what this means. Right now, the current plot is about the centralization of discourse on a few corporate platforms.","entities":["Russia","internet","Ukraine","globalization","Authoritarianism","democratic institutions","democracy-building efforts","Information Age","corporate platforms","Russia’s most recent invasion of Ukraine","Hitting the Books: We are the frogs in the boiling pot, it's time we started governing like it.","Engadget"],"facts":["Dissecting impact of Israel-Hamas conflict on markets -MENTIONS-> Russia","'Too big to fail' Egypt faces economic crisis but has an anti-Gaza refugee policy. Israel and the U.S. hope that will change -MENTIONS-> Russia","People are turning to Snap Map for firsthand perspectives from Gaza -MENTIONS-> Russia","Deepfake election risks trigger EU call for more generative AI safeguards -MENTIONS-> Russia","With hopes of victory fading, Ukraine's fight against Russia could get even harder in 2024 -MENTIONS-> Russia"]}

