{"title":"Today the FTX jury suffered through a code review (The Verge, 2023-10-06T22:21:46+00:00)","text":"Today the FTX jury suffered through a code review (The Verge, 2023-10-06T22:21:46+00:00)
Wang said he trusted Bankman-Fried’s judgment and didn’t pursue the issue further. Later, though, Alameda’s balance was more negative than FTT and the trading revenue, and Wang had more conversations with Bankman-Fried about it. Wang said he knew at the time that Alameda was using FTX’s customers’ funds and that he knew it was wrong.

We heard yesterday about the line of credit Alameda had on FTX, a staggering $65 billion. Today we saw it in the database. The line of credit didn’t start that big — Wang testified that Bankman-Fried had asked him to increase it a few times because Alameda kept running into its limits. First it was “a few hundred million,” then a billion, then even that wasn’t enough. It wasn’t clear how Wang arrived at $65 billion specifically, but he said he’d discussed the number with Bankman-Fried. Other customers didn’t have the same privileges.","entities":["Bankman-Fried","Alameda","FTT","FTX","Wang","Alameda's line of credit on FTX","Today the FTX jury suffered through a code review","The Verge"],"facts":["SBF’s trial starts soon, but how did he — and FTX — get here? -MENTIONS-> Bankman-Fried","In the end, the FTX trial was about the friends screwed along the way -MENTIONS-> Bankman-Fried","Sex, Signal messages, and sabotaging FTX's code: SBF execs and Bahamas roommates tell all in court -MENTIONS-> Bankman-Fried","Sam Altman backs teens’ startup, Google unveils the Pixel 8 and TikTok tests an ad-free tier -MENTIONS-> Bankman-Fried","Bankman-Fried -SAID-> Alameda Research"]}

{"title":"The FTX trial is bigger than Sam Bankman-Fried (The Verge, 2023-09-28T12:00:00+00:00)","text":"The FTX trial is bigger than Sam Bankman-Fried (The Verge, 2023-09-28T12:00:00+00:00)
We have some inkling of what the government will be arguing thanks to the filings prosecutors are making in this case. They argue that Bankman-Fried lied about consumer protection and that Bankman-Fried’s statements that FTX was “avoiding or managing conflicts of interest” and that “as a general principle FTX segregates customer assets from its own assets across our platforms” were lies, in a superseding indictment filed August 14th.

The indictment also says that there were special features in FTX’s code that “permitted Alameda to spend and withdraw unlimited amounts of money from FTX,” which were created at Bankman-Fried’s direction. That effectively exempted Alameda from the kinds of risk management other customers faced. At the same time, the government alleges, “Bankman-Fried publicly and repeatedly asserted that Alameda did not have privileged access to FTX.”","entities":["Alameda","risk management","consumer protection","conflicts of interest","superseding indictment","The FTX trial is bigger than Sam Bankman-Fried","FTX","Sam Bankman-Fried","government","The Verge"],"facts":["SBF’s trial starts soon, but how did he — and FTX — get here? -MENTIONS-> Alameda","SBF, riding high on FTX, reportedly offered $5B to Trump to cancel President re-run -MENTIONS-> Alameda","Is Sam Bankman-Fried a bad ‘man’ or a good ‘boy’? Lawyers swap opening statements before first witnesses take the stand -MENTIONS-> Alameda","The jury finally hears from Sam Bankman-Fried -MENTIONS-> Alameda","SBF Trial: The latest updates from the FTX collapse’s courtroom drama -MENTIONS-> Alameda"]}

{"title":"In the end, the FTX trial was about the friends screwed along the way (The Verge, 2023-10-26T12:00:00+00:00)","text":"In the end, the FTX trial was about the friends screwed along the way (The Verge, 2023-10-26T12:00:00+00:00)
It was turned on in July. No other customer trading on FTX had “allow_negative” privileges — only Alameda. Wang’s testimony suggests that the fraud at FTX started very early since the same day that allow_negative was switched on, Bankman-Fried tweeted that Alameda’s account “was like everyone else’s.”

The general sense I got, from the testimony of Bankman-Fried’s former friends, was that things just kept escalating. For instance, Alameda Research first had a negative balance in late 2019, Wang testified. Wang testified that he heard Bankman-Fried tell another trader that it was okay to continue withdrawing money from the account as long as the amount was less than FTX’s total trading revenue. A little later, Wang discovered that Alameda was negative by $50 million more than FTX’s revenue. Bankman-Fried told him it was fine, and it just didn’t account for the FTT token that the two of them had launched. Wang trusted him.","entities":["Bankman-Fried","Alameda Research","In the end, the FTX trial was about the friends screwed along the way","allow_negative","FTX trial","FTX","Wang","FTT token","fraud","The Verge"],"facts":["Sam Altman backs teens’ startup, Google unveils the Pixel 8 and TikTok tests an ad-free tier -MENTIONS-> Bankman-Fried","SBF’s trial starts soon, but how did he — and FTX — get here? -MENTIONS-> Bankman-Fried","Sex, Signal messages, and sabotaging FTX's code: SBF execs and Bahamas roommates tell all in court -MENTIONS-> Bankman-Fried","Today the FTX jury suffered through a code review -MENTIONS-> Bankman-Fried","Bankman-Fried -SAID-> Alameda"]}

